    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14249" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποφράς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>,
			ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> φράζω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not to be mentioned,
				unlucky;</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἡμέραι,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθαραὶ ἡμ.,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				800d
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				43.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Pseudol.</u>
				12
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πύλαι</span> at Rome, =
			<i>portae nefastae,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.518b
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> rarely as
			masc. Adj., <i>impious, wicked,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνθρωπος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eup.
					309
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Pseudol.</u>
					32
				</span></i>
			.</div>
